go.alis.build/sproto/v2 is deprecated in favour of go.alis.build/protodb/v2.

What it delivers: go get / go list -m -u show the module deprecation; gopls, staticcheck and
pkg.go.dev flag each package with its replacement.

Changes:
- go.mod: Go module deprecation comment directly above the module directive.
- Package docs gain a Deprecated paragraph (before the trailing link definitions):
  root -> protodb/v2 filtering + ordering, filtering -> protodb/v2/filtering,
  ordering -> protodb/v2/ordering. sproto/v2 has no table clients, so spanneradapter is not named.
- READMEs open with a one-line deprecation notice.

Files: sproto/v2/go.mod, sproto/v2/docs.go, sproto/v2/filtering/docs.go, sproto/v2/ordering/docs.go,
sproto/v2/README.md, sproto/v2/filtering/README.md, sproto/v2/ordering/README.md

Why: protodb/v2 absorbed these packages and already handles columns named after SQL keywords.
No behaviour change.
Checks: go doc prints each Deprecated paragraph; go mod edit -json shows Module.Deprecated;
go build ./... and go test ./... pass; gofmt clean on changed Go files.
